Use this:

> Continue G-ROUTE4 from the completed B′ main adjudication run on branch g-route4/adjudication.

Do not start A′ adjudication, Phase A′, Phase B′, qualification-table construction, or any new provider/model calls.

Your task is to help me resolve the 48 escalated B′ fixtures under the frozen adjudication rules.

For each escalated fixture:

read the sealed fixture, sealed gold, rationale, all available adjudicator verdicts, and sealed raw answers;

distinguish format-only disagreement from actual semantic/content disagreement;

do not unwrap, rescore, or reinterpret code-fenced JSON as a valid validator pass;

evaluate only the frozen derivability question: whether the sealed gold is uniquely justified by the fixture as written;

present one of the three allowed operator outcomes:

1. gold right → keep fixture;


2. gold wrong → fix gold;


3. input ambiguous → fix input;



give a short evidence-based reason for each recommendation;

do not change any fixture, gold, rationale, validator, threshold, or corpus file without my explicit per-fixture approval.


Triage the 48 into two groups first:

format-only escalations;

substantive content escalations.


Review the substantive-content group first, since those are the cases most likely to need an actual operator decision. Then review the format-only group.

Pay special attention to these four audit-sample fixtures:

B4-PLAN-R3-13

B4-RSRCH-R1-09

B4-RSRCH-R2-13

B4-RSRCH-R4-01


For each of those, explicitly state whether choosing gold wrong or input ambiguous would trigger the frozen full-cell consequence.

Before making any changes, produce a review table with:

fixture ID;

class / risk;

whether disagreement is format-only or substantive;

adjudicator verdict summary;

your recommended operator outcome;

reason;

whether a full-cell consequence would be triggered.


Stop after presenting the review table and wait for my decisions. Do not apply any fixes yet.

Approve gold right → keep for all four remaining fixed-fixture escalations:
B4-RSRCH-R2-06
B4-RSRCH-R2-14
B4-RSRCH-R3-14
B4-RSRCH-R3-18
Basis: each fixture has already used its one permitted input fix, all applicable re-checks passed, and every remaining adjudicator disagreement is format-only code-fenced JSON whose semantic content matches the fixed gold. Do not replace any of these fixtures.
Record the operator decisions with that rationale and close the B′ main adjudication batch.
Then produce a final B′ adjudication closure report containing:
total B′ fixtures;
number kept directly;
number fixed and then kept;
number replaced, if any;
number unresolved, if any;
number of provider sessions and retries;
any sampled/full-cell consequences triggered;
all known residual limitations, including the code-fence behavior and the latent-defect categories already documented.
Do not modify the sealed corpus, gold, validators, blueprint, audit sample, or thresholds.
Do not start A′ adjudication, Phase A′, Phase B′, qualification-table construction, or any other model calls.
Stop after the B′ adjudication stage is formally closed and report the exact commit hash.

Continue G-ROUTE4 from the formally closed B′ main adjudication stage at commit f07b1a2fa211ec2c4109117e2b5f1b5c742df7e2 on branch g-route4/adjudication.
The B′ stage is closed: 305/305 fixtures kept, 14 with recorded fixes, 0 replaced, 0 unresolved. Do not reopen or rescore B′.
Your next task is A′ adjudication only.
Requirements:
Use the sealed A′ corpus exactly as frozen, with no pre-editing of known latent defects.
Preserve the sealed corpus, gold, validators, blueprint, audit sample, thresholds, and seal tag.
Use the same amended O2 adjudication configuration and the same committed exactly-once harness/integrity rules already used for B′.
Every A′ fixture must receive the full frozen adjudication treatment required by the design.
Commit and push every adjudicator answer set before comparing it with gold.
Do not unwrap or reinterpret code-fenced JSON as a valid validator pass. Diagnostic comparison of fenced content is allowed only to distinguish format disagreement from semantic disagreement, exactly as in B′.
Do not silently repair the known latent P6 or SY1 defects before adjudication. Let them surface under the frozen rules.
If a fixture escalates, stop at the point where the frozen protocol requires my operator decision. Do not choose gold right, gold wrong, or input ambiguous on my behalf.
If a fixture is approved for an input fix later, apply only its one permitted minimal fix, rerun all frozen checks, and re-adjudicate from scratch.
Do not start the G-ROUTE4 Phase A′ qualification run, build a qualification table, start Phase B′, or make any unrelated provider/model calls.
Before the first A′ provider call, verify and report:
current branch and commit;
seal and blueprint bindings;
A′ fixture count and schedule;
adjudicator configuration digest;
harness/test status;
that no B′ artifact is being reopened or modified.
Then run the A′ adjudication batch.
When the batch reaches an operator-decision boundary, report:
total A′ fixtures;
total adjudicator sessions;
direct keeps;
escalations;
format-only disagreements;
substantive disagreements;
any known latent-defect fixtures that surfaced;
any integrity/retry issues;
exact commits/digests for sealed answers and scores.
Stop there and wait for my decisions.
Do not proceed into experimental qualification or routing execution.

Approve the A′ operator decisions from your read-only review.

Record `gold right → keep` for these 20 fixtures:

- all 19 format-only escalations exactly as listed in your review;
- `A4-PLAN-R3-04`.

Basis:
- for the 19 format-only cases, every disagreement is code-fenced JSON whose semantic content matches gold;
- for `A4-PLAN-R3-04`, the sealed fixture and gold are uniquely derivable and pass the frozen validators, while the three provider safety refusals provide no evidence against fixture or gold validity.

Record `input ambiguous → fix input` for these 6 fixtures:

- `A4-RSRCH-R2-02`
- `A4-RSRCH-R4-03`
- `A4-SYNTH-R2-03`
- `A4-SYNTH-R4-01`
- `A4-EXTR-R1-03`
- `A4-RSRCH-R2-01`

Apply only the minimal repairs established in the review:

- For `A4-RSRCH-R2-02` and `A4-RSRCH-R4-03`, remove the exclusionary `only` wording while preserving the intended P6 narrower-scope construct and all unaffected frozen features.
- For `A4-SYNTH-R2-03` and `A4-SYNTH-R4-01`, relabel the causal observation as the required `finding`, with the corresponding symptom observation relabelled as needed so the frozen observation count, roles, mergeability, family and feature constraints remain satisfied. Update derived gold roles only; do not change the conclusion or required terms.
- For `A4-EXTR-R1-03`, rename the undefined field `venue` to `town`, preserving the gold value `Dalihi`, field count, type structure, derived-field count and all other frozen features.
- For `A4-RSRCH-R2-01`, minimally rewrite the supporting source wording so it actually supports the claim that collection occurs every Saturday, and update the matching reissue consistently while preserving all other frozen research features.

For each of the six fixes:
1. bind the fix to the sealed fixture and gold digests;
2. preserve every unaffected frozen feature;
3. rerun all applicable structural, independence, O6, cap and fixture checks;
4. treat this as the fixture’s one allowed fix;
5. re-adjudicate from scratch using the full frozen A′ treatment of three adjudicators;
6. commit and push all adjudicator answers before comparing them with gold;
7. if all three agree, keep the fixture;
8. if they do not all agree, return to me for an operator decision before any replacement.

Do not alter any of the 20 kept fixtures.

Preserve the known-latent-defect disclosures, including the newly noted weak courier paraphrase in `B4-RSRCH-R2-X04`. Do not edit reserves proactively.

Do not begin qualification-table construction, Phase A′, Phase B′, or any unrelated provider calls.

When the six fix rounds finish, report:
- validation results for each fix;
- all adjudicator outcomes;
- which fixtures kept automatically;
- which, if any, return for operator decision;
- session/retry/integrity counts;
- exact commits and digests.

Stop there.
